<http://data.silknow.org/object/b8e89245-ff4b-32e5-bbe7-87eff0b51f9b/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Man’s court waistcoat with a 2-inch (5 cm) standing collar, straight fronts and skirts reaching to the top of the hip. There are no pockets, only a pointed pocket flap on each front.  The fronts and pocket flaps are made of ivory silk twill, the back of linen.  The waistcoat is lined with linen; the front skirts are ivory silk twill, and the front facings ivory silk taffeta. The waistcoat is appliquéd with white silk cord and embroidered-to-shape with silk floss in yellow and shades of green, blue and pink in a pattern of flowers and leaves with a trellised border, on the pocket flaps, collar and along the front edges and hems.  The fronts are embroidered with repeating floral sprigs.  There are 8 worked buttonholes along the left front with 5 (3 missing) embroidered buttons on the right front."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/b8e89245-ff4b-32e5-bbe7-87eff0b51f9b> .

